From 0057683222efec3e2f4a51c30cef8bdf56ea819b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:32:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(web-scan): owe pending rechecks, keep the list on
 typed starts, persist the rescan block

Review of a104be8 on #70:

- H1: withOwedRechecks also owes the block of any match whose receipt is
  'pending' below the saved nextBlock, retried or not. A genuine router
  payment whose recheck found real but not-yet-final evidence (a head drop,
  a provider switch) was in 'retried' and below the floor, so neither the
  list nor the pending rule held it. It stays capped by RECHECK_MAX and is
  counted in any overflow; pending needs a real router transfer, so spam
  cannot pin the list with it.
- M1: a typed start (Resume unchecked) copies checkpoint.recheck and
  checkpoint.rescanFrom into its cursor, so owed blocks below the typed
  start keep their one retry (owedRechecks drops entries >= nextBlock).
- M2: ScanCursor.rescanFrom persists the rescan block of an overflow
  (decimal string, validated < nextBlock on load; a malformed value is
  dropped and the rest of the cursor kept; old checkpoints load unchanged).
  It is carried on every save while the run starts above it, a lower block
  wins over a new overflow's, and a run starting at or below it clears it
  on save. The Scan view shows the notice from the stored checkpoint too,
  with the new count-neutral critical key scan.recheck.overflowSaved
  (en source, es/ja/ar machine drafts).
- M3: restores the direct-cursor case recheck [120, 120, SETTLED, HEAD]:
  single-block reads are exactly [120], so the '< nextBlock' filter of
  owedRechecks is pinned again (mutation X1 now fails).
- withOwedRechecks JSDoc documents the accepted spam case: with 9 or more
  always-failing router claims, following the notice cannot clear it (no
  funds lost).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
